{"ts":"2026-08-13T22:21:57.212Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"96c82b014efa1c027a8463f2","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-13T22:21:57.212Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-08-13T22:21:57.199Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-08-13T22:21:57.199Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Fixed: runTodoImport now attaches a traceable close reason (Imported as <status> from <file> line <n>) whenever it creates or upserts an item into a terminal status, so checked [x] lines land in the tracker instead of being rejected by the default governance.require_close_reason policy. Partial-import contract chosen: import what it can, then report every dropped line in a structured 'dropped' array on the normal output path (stdout JSON) and set a non-zero process exit code via withDroppedReport (used by the todos importer, todos-import legacy importer, and todos sync). sync refuses to overwrite the source file when the import half dropped a line, preserving the original bytes. Verified by 8 tests (4 end-to-end via real pm subprocess, 4 in-process unit) all run green through pm test --run; release:check passes."}],"before_hash":"4234e5e804f895108254edfd0d090e59bb5c4967ef330fe11f9d638466ab8e59","after_hash":"2826ba390827124cb26f7d3298a4551548542f1fb491c70cfb4b0a50a698c549"}
